_Yemen_in_Sana%27a.JPG","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Bab_Al_Yemen_in_Sana%27a.JPG","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"User: (WT-shared) Shoestring at wts wikivoyage","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bab_Al_Yemen_in_Sana%27a.JPG"}},{"id":"sanaa_old_sana_a","areaId":"sanaa","name":"Old Sana'a","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":15.35556,"lng":44.20806},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"sanaa_old_sana_a","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.sanaacity.com/","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":29,"commonsNearby":101,"wikiPageviews":136,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["oldsanaa","sanaa"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Old City of Sanaʽa is a recognised UNESCO World Heritage Site in the Amanat Al Asimah Governorate, Yemen. As of 2003, the district had a population of 63,398 inhabitants. The old fortified city has been inhabited for more than 2,500 years and contains many intact architectural sites.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Old City of Sana'a","unesco":true,"photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/View_of_Old_Sana%27a%2C_Yemen%2C_Jan._2009.jpg/1280px-View_of_Old_Sana%27a%2C_Yemen%2C_Jan._2009.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/View_of_Old_Sana%27a%2C_Yemen%2C_Jan._2009.jpg/500px-View_of_Old_Sana%27a%2C_Yemen%2C_Jan._2009.jpg","w":1200,"h":814,"author":"Ferdinand Reus from Arnhem, Holland","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Old_Sana%27a,_Yemen,_Jan._2009.jpg"}},{"id":"sanaa_ghumdan_palace","areaId":"sanaa","name":"Ghumdan Palace","category":"monument","tags":["history","art"],"location":{"lat":15.353,"lng":44.21442},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"sanaa_ghumdan_palace","tickets":[],"sign